User turn 1:
Write a simple website in HTML. When a user clicks the button, it shows a random joke from a list of 4 jokes.

Response A, turn 1:
```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Joke Picker</title>
<body><button id="pick">Tell me a joke</button><p id="joke" aria-live="polite"></p>
<script>
const jokes = [
  'Why did the scarecrow win an award? He was outstanding in his field.',
  'Why was six afraid of seven? Because seven eight nine.',
  'What do you call fake spaghetti? An impasta.',
  'Why do programmers prefer dark mode? Light attracts bugs.'
];
document.querySelector('#pick').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const i = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
  document.querySelector('#joke').textContent = jokes[i];
});
</script></body></html>
```

